  "caption": "Figure 1: The overall process of Subgraph Matching is a search algorithm that matches one node pair at a time for the input query q and target graph G guided by a learned policy. Due to the large action space incurred by the large G in practice, we propose to train a policy network to guide the selection of local candidate nodes in G at each search state. This requires effective node embeddings to be learned that can reflect the node-to-node mapping at the current state and contribute to the prediction of the policy and reward. To achieve this end, we propose a novel QC-SGMNN encoder layer consisting of a “Propagation” module that performs intra-graph message passing as a typical GNN and a “Matching” module that performs state-dependent inter-graph matching (Section 3.2.1). The Pθ(at|st) is trained using the novel loss functions described in Section 3.1.",
